note 2026-11-09T13:50:00Z
    **Decision (agent, 2026-11-09):** migration reset is per record, not per definition (narrows the user's migration
    Q1 A). **Why:** resetting records that still decode loses data for no safety gain (OD54 (8)). **Reverse:** reset
    every record of the definition when any is incompatible. **Governs:** @spec.Restore.
note 2026-11-09T13:51:00Z
    **Decision (agent, 2026-11-09):** any structural Schema change to a stored field resets the record, even a harmless
    one, so an offline app loses saved drafts, and a changed computed initial value resets too, until computed fields
    are derived on restore (Q19). **Why:** a fixed rule `flow explain --since` can list before a deploy (OD54 (9)).
    **Reverse:** reset only when the old value fails to decode. **Governs:** @spec.Restore, @spec.Codec.
note 2026-11-09T13:53:00Z
    **Decision (agent, 2026-11-09):** a dropped field is applied at that release's boot, rewriting the records holding
    it (Q20), a bounded exception to D111. **Why:** a later re-add starts empty, not with resurrected data (OD54 (10)).
    **Reverse:** keep D111 strict. **Governs:** @spec.Restore.
note 2026-11-09T13:54:00Z
    **Decision (agent, 2026-11-09):** a new identity gets its own lane (Q17); the old identity's in-flight write is
    kept, blocks nothing, is reported at every boot and ends only by its own answer; `forget` does not release it.
    **Why:** a lane is (identity, contract, key) (OD54 (7)). **Reverse:** needs a new word (an identity route), the
    user's API call. **Governs:** @spec.WriteLanes, @spec.Restore.
note 2026-11-09T13:55:00Z
    **Decision (agent, 2026-11-09):** the repair bound resets at `RepairOverdue`: 3 asks, then `RepairOverdue`, then the
    count starts again. **Why:** a doubt on a long-open screen is never stranded (stage A close-out B1, `d3d89576`).
    **Reverse:** one rule. **Governs:** @plan.EntityDomains.
note 2026-11-09T13:56:00Z
    **Decision (agent, 2026-11-09):** two write operations on one contract stay illegal (`SharedContract`, a
    `flow check` error). **Why:** the design forbids them (F2; B2). **Reverse:** allowing them reverses F2 and needs
    design work. **Governs:** @spec.Compile, @spec.StaticCli.
note 2026-11-09T13:57:00Z
    **Decision (agent, 2026-11-09):** entities under `guarded` (OD52 (1), (6), (9), (10), (14)): a doubt ends only on
    proof; the record queue is released once the forced repair settles; `Released` frees a never-re-sent unknown's
    queue entry; U10's later success is by landing order; no `allOrNothing`. **Why:** one actor's hold blocks no other.
    **Reverse:** one rule each in rules 30 and 32. **Governs:** @plan.EntityDomains.
note 2026-11-09T13:58:00Z
    **Decision (agent, 2026-11-09):** streams (OD53): `emit.fail(e, key)` on `Feed.multiplex`; a key change empties a
    `fills` field in the same turn (`FillsOtherKey`); a session's select runs every committed turn; backoff 500 ms x
    2^n, jittered, capped at 30 s; 256 bookmarks per operation; T1 wins over T5 on Waiting; `dropAt` set on leaving
    Live or Repairing; `Feed.callback`'s 1,024 bound counts the queue only; `SelectedNoKey`. **Why:** OD53, audits S1,
    S1b. **Reverse:** one rule or constant each. **Governs:** @plan.Operations.
note 2026-11-09T13:59:00Z
    **Decision (agent, 2026-11-09):** rounds 15, 15b and area H (OD50, OD51): `cancelAll` interrupts a head on the wire
    and delivers the queue first, the hold-leaving head last; rule 15's cancel exemption dropped; `forget` removes the
    record and a held lane stays unbound and reported; an Effect default is a construction error; R2, R6, R7, R8, R10
    and M2 as in `prototypes/round-14/STATUS.md`. **Why:** OD50, OD51. **Reverse:** one rule each. **Governs:**
